---
import TextPage from '../components/TextPage.astro';
import { SITE } from '../lib/site';
export const prerender = true;
---

<TextPage
  title="Privacy Policy"
  eyebrow="Legal"
  description={`How ${SITE.name} collects, uses and protects your personal information.`}
>
  <p><strong>Last updated:</strong> September 28, 2026</p>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} (“we”, “us”, “our”) runs loopedbyhand.com, a free library of crochet patterns. This policy explains
    what information we collect when you visit the site, why we collect it, and the choices you have. We keep things
    simple: we collect as little as possible and we never sell your data.
  </p>

  <h2>Information we collect</h2>
  <h3>Information you give us</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Newsletter sign-up:</strong> your email address and the date you subscribed, only if you choose to join
      the newsletter.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Contact form:</strong> your name, email address and the message you write, only if you send us a message.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>Information collected automatically</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Hosting data:</strong> the site is hosted on Cloudflare. Like any web host, Cloudflare processes standard
      technical data (such as your IP address, browser type and the pages requested) to deliver the site and protect it
      from abuse and attacks.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fonts:</strong> our typefaces are loaded from Google Fonts, so your browser connects to Google’s servers,
      which receive your IP address when the page loads.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Cookies and tracking</h2>
  <p>
    We do not use advertising cookies, tracking pixels or third-party analytics, and we don’t build profiles about
    visitors. If we ever add analytics or advertising, we’ll update this policy first and ask for consent where the law
    requires it.
  </p>

  <h2>How we use your information</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>To send you the newsletter you signed up for, with news about new patterns.</li>
    <li>To read and reply to messages you send us.</li>
    <li>To keep the site secure, working properly and free of spam.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Our legal basis is your <strong>consent</strong> (newsletter and contact form) and our <strong>legitimate
    interest</strong> in running a safe, working website (hosting and security data).
  </p>

  <h2>Sharing your information</h2>
  <p>
    We don’t sell, rent or trade your personal information. We only share it with the service providers that help us
    run the site. Cloudflare hosts the site and stores our database, and Google Fonts delivers our typefaces. We may
    also disclose information if the law requires us to.
  </p>

  <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Newsletter emails are kept until you unsubscribe.</li>
    <li>Contact messages are kept only as long as needed to answer you, and are then deleted.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your rights</h2>
  <p>Depending on where you live (for example under the GDPR or CCPA), you may have the right to:</p>
  <ul>
    <li>ask for a copy of the personal information we hold about you;</li>
    <li>ask us to correct or delete it;</li>
    <li>withdraw your consent and unsubscribe from the newsletter at any time;</li>
    <li>object to or restrict how we use your information;</li>
    <li>complain to your local data-protection authority.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>To use any of these rights, just <a href="/contact">send us a message</a>. We’ll reply within 30 days.</p>

  <h2>Security</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served over HTTPS, and our database can only be reached by the site itself. No method of storing data
    online is 100% secure, but we take reasonable steps to protect your information.
  </p>

  <h2>Children</h2>
  <p>
    {SITE.name} is not directed at children under 13, and we don’t knowingly collect their personal information. If you
    believe a child has sent us their details, please <a href="/contact">contact us</a> and we’ll delete them.
  </p>

  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>
    Patterns may link to yarn shops or other websites. We’re not responsible for their privacy practices, so please
    read their policies too.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes to this policy</h2>
  <p>
    We may update this policy from time to time. When we do, we’ll change the “Last updated” date above. Significant
    changes will be announced on the site or in the newsletter.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p>
    Questions about your privacy? Reach {SITE.author} through the <a href="/contact">contact page</a>.
  </p>
</TextPage>
